{"reference":"1 Chronicles 17","book":"1 Chronicles","chapter":17,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"David’s House and the Temple","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The chapter reverses David’s proposal: David wants to build a house for the LORD, but the LORD promises to build David a “house,” meaning an enduring royal line. Nathan announces that one of David’s sons will build the temple and that his throne will be established. The promise also describes a father-son relationship and speaks of discipline for wrongdoing, while David responds by praying that the promise concerning his house will stand.","verse_refs":["1 Chronicles 17:1-27"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_1_chronicles_017_24483d09360884c9b924ae3a","reader_path_1_chronicles_017_57d4aeb5bb26f184b498a8ff"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}